<<~ ahu slot=`#/body`>>

Terra-Tier-Source: Lares (Tasked Spirit). Read-only design read. Repo: /home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine at ffe05bc79. Write nothing. Mark claims MEASURED (file:line) or INFER.
Context: /home/joshu/.lares-scratch/controller/terra-unwired-depth/final.md (your earlier read, Q3/Q4) and bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/cap-tier.mem + reach-plane.mem. A builder lane now wires the declared cap-tier and the CONTRACT secrets floor onto every live crossing (node repo share, browser repo share, node bulb read face, node CAS block door).
Design, from the code:
# A production DeclaredTierSource: how a documentId AND a CAS CID each resolve to their bag and its declared tier (bag manifests, bag-manifest.ts ~81; the per-tiddler cascade cap-tier.mem names; the bag registry). Where does a CID learn its bag? What reads torn/absent, and what must that verdict be (fail closed vs inert)?
# ONE reusable tightening predicate: its signature, and the exact insertion point at each allowing return of the four surfaces (list each return by file:line), so a structural deny never loosens and sibling/in-process paths get the right answer (does a same-face sibling ever need tightening? does in-process?).
# The durable secrets registry: where in the per-face sealed catalog (packages/lararium-node, the sealed store) a secrets-plane record fits, how the boot reads it before the first share verdict, and what refuses when it cannot be read.
# The reds that must fail first, one per surface plus restart and omission.
Final message under 900 words.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/seat-law`>>

!! SEAT LAW (appended by tools/launch-codex.mjs to every brief; it binds this seat)
* A lane launches no Sol seat; the controller's one Sol read per train runs at the read floor of 0%.
* Stay inside the wall. Approval never escalates; a build seat has no network, loopback included; only a research seat takes `--search`. A step that needs more than the wall stops and names itself in `out.md`; the wall holds by refusal.
* Never commit and never run a git write. The lead commits each red, then each fix.
* Never build (`pnpm build`), never run vitest browser mode, never stand a vessel, socket or daemon. Typecheck (`tsc -p … --noEmit`) and run single test files that open no socket; mark any test that needs a socket "lead runs".
* A "stale build" from the dist guard stops the run; name it, and the lead builds.
* A read seat writes no file: its final message carries the hand-back. Any other seat writes `out.md` and every note in the seat directory alone. `-o` names `final.md`; stdin closes (`< /dev/null`); `TMPDIR` and `TMPPREFIX` sit inside the seat directory.
* Never run the battery; the lead holds its lock. Never read a credential file.
* Launch without `--ephemeral`: each seat keeps its rollout, so the spend tally counts it.
* The lead runs `pnpm build` in its worktree after every span merge and before each build seat; a verdict read off a stale dist counts as unread.

<<~/ahu>>

